{
  "$comment": "Campaign level 42 (chapter 4, The Wild Heart): a dry grassland under golden light. Home hills west, a walled aggressive tribe on a sheer bluff east (disc aboveSea 100, falloff 2, sealed until objective 4 raises a nine step ramp), the sneaky hill tribe on a sealed southern hill (opened by a seven step ramp at objective 3), and a dormant reliquary with an unheld dormant ward stone in mid field. Stages: raise a Warden Lodge (start with 8 followers; until it stands, 4 bluff wardens march on the Hearth every 120 s from 480 s, the idle loss); raise a Fire Lodge; break the 10 warden and 4 firecaller guard posted at the ward stone and pray it; pray 60 s with six at the reliquary while hill raiders (3 every 110 s) come for the worshippers; kill fourteen of the hill tribe after its ramp rises (4 raiders every 120 s go for the ward stone); climb the bluff ramp and burn the rival Hearth (10 plus 8 posted wardens, 4 firecallers, 3 towers, maxTroops 14; war bands for the ward stone 30 s after the ramp and every 150 s). From the ward stone on, neutral Fire Rain falls on the roads to the reliquary every 130 s (south lane, south track, west road halfway home, east road by the ward stone), each warned 10 s ahead, until the win; the points sit 10 to 30 cells from the reliquary so the knockback never throws worshippers out of the ring. The hill raids after the reliquary are four one shot bands of 4 (16 for a kill goal of 14), so the goal stays possible if the hill tribe falls early. Hard bot offset 1 wins at tick 30016 (stages done at 2802, 4934, 9810, 13917, 15472); offsets 0 to 5 win 26947 to 40544. Time limit 3600 s (72000 ticks, over 2x the bot).",
